From: clearbluejar <3752074+clearbluejar@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 10:43:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] 10025: Decompiler: number default local variable names per
 name base

The default names the decompiler assigns to local variables (uVar1, iVar2,
pcVar3, ...) were numbered from a single counter shared across all
data-types. Adding or removing one variable anywhere in a function
therefore renumbered every variable named after it, which produces large
spurious diffs when comparing the decompiler output of two versions of a
function.

Number the names independently for each name base instead, using the
smallest index not already taken in the local scope (uVar1, uVar2, ...
iVar1, iVar2, ...). A change to the variables of one data-type no longer
renumbers variables of other data-types.

Diffing afd.sys 10.0.22621.1028 against .1415 (1152 matched functions),
the changed lines caused only by variable renumbering drop from 2310 to
966 and the total changed lines from 10218 to 8875. Output is otherwise
unchanged apart from line wrapping that follows from shorter names.
Decompiler datatests pass as before; DecompilerFindDialogTest updated for
the new numbering.
---
 .../Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/database.cc  | 23 ++++----
 .../decompile/cpp/include/ghidra/database.hh  |  3 +-
 .../decompile/DecompilerFindDialogTest.java   | 54 +++++++++----------
 3 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 40 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/database.cc b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/database.cc
index 8993cd9c04..484d98a5d1 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/database.cc
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/database.cc
@@ -2684,20 +2684,19 @@ string ScopeInternal::buildVariableName(const Address &addr,
       s << "var";
   }
   else {			// Some sort of local variable
+    // Default names are numbered independently for each name base (uVar1, uVar2, ... iVar1, iVar2, ...)
+    // rather than from a single counter shared across all data-types.  Adding or removing a variable
+    // of one data-type then does not renumber variables of other data-types, which keeps the default
+    // names stable when comparing output across related functions (i.e. diffing two versions of a binary).
     if (ct != (Datatype *)0)
       ct->printNameBase(s);
-    s << "Var" << dec << index++;
-    if (findFirstByName(s.str()) != nametree.end()) {	// If the name already exists
-      for(int4 i=0;i<10;++i) {	// Try bumping up the index a few times before calling makeNameUnique
-	ostringstream s2;
-	if (ct != (Datatype *)0)
-	  ct->printNameBase(s2);
-	s2 << "Var" << dec << index++;
-	if (findFirstByName(s2.str()) == nametree.end()) {
-	  return s2.str();
-	}
-      }
-    }
+    s << "Var";
+    string prefix = s.str();
+    int4 i = 1;
+    string nm = prefix + to_string(i);
+    while(findFirstByName(nm) != nametree.end())	// Use the smallest index not already taken for this name base
+      nm = prefix + to_string(++i);
+    return nm;
   }
   return makeNameUnique(s.str());
 }
diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/include/ghidra/database.hh b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/include/ghidra/database.hh
index 3725597b17..f5e4df8f47 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/include/ghidra/database.hh
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/src/decompile/cpp/include/ghidra/database.hh
@@ -763,7 +763,8 @@ public:
   /// \param addr is the given address
   /// \param pc is the address at which the name is getting used
   /// \param ct is a data-type used to inform the name
-  /// \param index is a reference to an index used to make the name unique, which will be updated
+  /// \param index is the parameter index for a function parameter (negative for an \e irregular input);
+  ///        default names for other local variables are numbered independently for each name base
   /// \param flags are boolean properties of the variable we need the name for
   /// \return the new variable name
   virtual string buildVariableName(const Address &addr,
